orbital behaviour and the nebular formation model.\",\n    \"principle\": \"For bodies orbiting the same central mass: T² ∝ a³\",\n    \"concept\": \"solar\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"solar\",\n      \"solar system explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"geophysics-tectonics\",\n    \"route\": \"/geophysics/tectonics\",\n    \"subject\": \"Geophysics\",\n    \"title\": \"Plate tectonics\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore plates, boundaries, magnetic stripes, triple junctions and Earth’s shape.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Plate motion links surface patterns and geological processes\",\n    \"concept\": \"tectonics\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"tectonics\",\n      \"plate tectonics\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-damped-oscillator\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/damped-oscillator\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Damped oscillator\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how damping changes oscillations and the approach to equilibrium.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A damping force removes mechanical energy\",\n    \"concept\": \"oscillation\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"damped oscillator\",\n      \"damped oscillator\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"gamma\",\n        \"label\": \"Damping γ\",\n        \"unit\": \"1/s\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 6,\n        \"default\": 0.8\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"omega0\",\n        \"label\": \"Natural frequency ω₀\",\n        \"unit\": \"rad/s\",\n        \"min\": 0.5,\n        \"max\": 6,\n        \"default\": 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"y0\",\n        \"label\": \"Initial displacement y(0)\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": -2,\n        \"max\": 2,\n        \"default\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"yp0\",\n        \"label\": \"Initial velocity y'(0)\",\n        \"unit\": \"/s\",\n        \"min\": -4,\n        \"max\": 4,\n        \"default\": 0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-div-stokes\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/div-stokes\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Divergence and Stokes theorems\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare local derivative descriptions with flux and circulation integrals.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Volume divergence corresponds to closed-surface flux\",\n    \"concept\": \"calculus\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"div stokes\",\n      \"divergence and stokes theorems\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"disk.r\",\n        \"label\": \"disk.r\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.4,\n        \"max\": 2.2,\n        \"default\": 1.1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-eigenvector-explorer\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/eigenvector-explorer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Eigenvector explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore directions preserved by a linear transformation.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Av = λv for a nonzero eigenvector v\",\n    \"concept\": \"matrix\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"eigenvector explorer\",\n      \"eigenvector explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"t\",\n        \"label\": \"t\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 1,\n        \"default\": 1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-fourier-series\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/fourier-series\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Fourier series\",\n    \"description\": \"Build a periodic signal from harmonic components.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A periodic signal can be represented by harmonic sums under suitable conditions\",\n    \"concept\": \"fourier\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"fourier series\",\n      \"fourier series\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"n\",\n        \"label\": \"n\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 1,\n        \"max\": 60,\n        \"default\": 1,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-fourier-transform\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/fourier-transform\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Fourier transform\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare a signal with its frequency-domain representation.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Frequency-domain structure describes a signal’s component frequencies\",\n    \"concept\": \"fourier\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"fourier transform\",\n      \"fourier transform\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"a\",\n        \"label\": \"a\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.2,\n        \"max\": 3,\n        \"default\": 1\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-gamma-function\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/gamma-function\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Gamma function\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how the gamma function extends factorials beyond positive integers.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Γ(n) = (n−1)! for positive integers n\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"gamma function\",\n      \"gamma function\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-gradient-explorer\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/gradient-explorer\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Gradient explorer\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore how a scalar field changes and how its gradient points uphill.\",\n    \"principle\": \"∇f points in the direction of greatest local increase\",\n    \"concept\": \"calculus\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"gradient explorer\",\n      \"gradient explorer\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-hermite-laguerre-delta\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/hermite-laguerre-delta\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Hermite, Laguerre and delta\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore special functions and finite-width representations of a delta distribution.\",\n    \"principle\": \"A delta distribution is defined through its action under integration\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"hermite laguerre delta\",\n      \"hermite, laguerre and delta\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"epsExp\",\n        \"label\": \"epsExp\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": -2,\n        \"max\": 0.3,\n        \"default\": 0\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"minitab-legendre-bessel\",\n    \"route\": \"/minitab/legendre-bessel\",\n    \"subject\": \"Mathematics\",\n    \"title\": \"Legendre and Bessel functions\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore special-function solutions that arise in problems with symmetry.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Boundary conditions select physically relevant solutions\",\n    \"concept\": \"special\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"legendre bessel\",\n      \"legendre and bessel functions\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"besX\",\n        \"label\": \"besX\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0.5,\n        \"max\": 14.5,\n        \"default\": 5\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-skeletal-system\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/skeletal-system\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Human skeletal system\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore the major bones and groups, their locations and functions. A typical adult has 206 bones: 80 axial and 126 appendicular. Group counts are not counts of SVG shapes. Identification and classification challenges support classroom discussion.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Axial (80) + appendicular (126) = 206 bones in a typical adult. Bones support, protect and act as levers.\",\n    \"concept\": \"skeleton\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"skeletal system\",\n      \"human skeleton\",\n      \"skeleton\",\n      \"bones\",\n      \"femur\",\n      \"skull\",\n      \"axial skeleton\",\n      \"appendicular skeleton\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"boneIndex\",\n        \"label\": \"Bone/group index in the activity list\",\n        \"unit\": \"\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 23,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"view\",\n        \"default\": \"front\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"front\",\n          \"back\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"division\",\n        \"default\": \"all\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"all\",\n          \"axial\",\n          \"appendicular\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"labels\",\n        \"default\": \"on\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"on\",\n          \"off\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"activity\",\n        \"default\": \"explore\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"explore\",\n          \"identify\",\n          \"classify\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-cells\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/cells\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Cells and organelles\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare plant and animal cell structures and explain selected organelle functions.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Compare plant and animal cell structures and explain selected organelle functions.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-cells\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"cells\",\n      \"cell organelles\",\n      \"plant cell\",\n      \"animal cell\",\n      \"cellular biology\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 7,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"cell\",\n        \"default\": \"plant\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"plant\",\n          \"animal\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"labels\",\n        \"default\": \"on\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"on\",\n          \"off\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"cellView\",\n        \"default\": \"illustration\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"illustration\",\n          \"microscope\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-mitosis\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/mitosis\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Mitosis and the cell cycle\",\n    \"description\": \"Track one replication and one division, preserving chromosome set number.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Track one replication and one division, preserving chromosome set number.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-mitosis\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"mitosis\",\n      \"cell cycle\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 5,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-meiosis\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/meiosis\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Meiosis and genetic variation\",\n    \"description\": \"Track homologues then sister chromatids through two divisions and explore genetic variation.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Track homologues then sister chromatids through two divisions and explore genetic variation.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-meiosis\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"meiosis\",\n      \"meiotic division\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 8,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"crossing\",\n        \"default\": \"on\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"on\",\n          \"off\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"orientation\",\n        \"default\": \"original\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"original\",\n          \"alternate\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-transpiration\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/transpiration\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Transpiration in plants\",\n    \"description\": \"Explore humidity, air movement, temperature and stomatal opening with an illustrative relative water-loss index.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Explore humidity, air movement, temperature and stomatal opening with an illustrative relative water-loss index.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-transpiration\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"transpiration\",\n      \"plant water loss\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 3,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"humidity\",\n        \"label\": \"Humidity\",\n        \"unit\": \"%\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 100,\n        \"default\": 50\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"wind\",\n        \"label\": \"Air movement\",\n        \"unit\": \"relative\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 5,\n        \"default\": 1\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"temperature\",\n        \"label\": \"Temperature\",\n        \"unit\": \"°C\",\n        \"min\": 10,\n        \"max\": 40,\n        \"default\": 25\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"opening\",\n        \"label\": \"Stomatal opening\",\n        \"unit\": \"%\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 100,\n        \"default\": 100\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-classification\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/classification\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Classification and scientific names\",\n    \"description\": \"Search and compare 90 organisms across Domain and KPCOFGS, inspect source notes and practise scientific names.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Compare human and domestic cat ranks from Domain to Species and practise scientific names.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-classification\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"classification\",\n      \"taxonomy\",\n      \"KPCOFGS\",\n      \"nomenclature\",\n      \"binomial naming\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 7,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"organismIndex\",\n        \"label\": \"First organism\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 89,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"key\": \"comparisonIndex\",\n        \"label\": \"Comparison organism\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 89,\n        \"default\": 1,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"labels\",\n        \"default\": \"on\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"on\",\n          \"off\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"protected\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"biology-life-processes\",\n    \"route\": \"/biology/life-processes\",\n    \"subject\": \"Biology\",\n    \"title\": \"Characteristics of living things\",\n    \"description\": \"Examine evidence for life, compare life processes and distinguish common misconceptions.\",\n    \"principle\": \"Examine evidence for life, compare life processes and distinguish common misconceptions.\",\n    \"concept\": \"bio-life-processes\",\n    \"aliases\": [\n      \"life processes\",\n      \"characteristics of living things\",\n      \"MRNIGERDCA\",\n      \"MRS GREN\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": [\n      {\n        \"key\": \"step\",\n        \"label\": \"Stage or structure\",\n        \"unit\": \"index\",\n        \"min\": 0,\n        \"max\": 9,\n        \"default\": 0,\n        \"integer\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"modes\": [],\n    \"protected\": false\n  }\n]\n"}, "src/lib/biology/reference-images.json": {"encoding": "utf8", "content": "{\n  \"cells\": {\n    \"plant-cell\": {\n      \"src\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Plant_cell_structure-en.svg/960px-Plant_cell_structure-en.svg.png\",\n      \"width\": 960,\n      \"height\": 703,\n      \"title\": \"Plant cell structure-en.svg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Scientific illustration\",\n      \"artist\": \"LadyofHats (Mariana Ruiz)\",\n      \"license\": \"Public domain\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plant_cell_structure-en.svg\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plant_cell_structure-en.svg\",\n      \"description\": \"Detailed labelled plant-cell cutaway. Labels and colours are illustrative, not microscope observations.\"\n    },\n    \"animal-cell\": {\n      \"src\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Animal_cell_structure_en.svg/960px-Animal_cell_structure_en.svg.png\",\n      \"width\": 960,\n      \"height\": 641,\n      \"title\": \"Animal cell structure en.svg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Scientific illustration\",\n      \"artist\": \"LadyofHats (Mariana Ruiz)\",\n      \"license\": \"Public domain\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animal_cell_structure_en.svg\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Animal_cell_structure_en.svg\",\n      \"description\": \"Detailed labelled animal-cell cutaway. Labels and colours are illustrative, not microscope observations.\"\n    },\n    \"plant-micrograph\": {\n      \"src\": \"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Elodea_cells_under_microscope.jpg/500px-Elodea_cells_under_microscope.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 500,\n      \"height\": 667,\n      \"title\": \"Elodea cells under microscope.jpg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Light micrograph\",\n      \"artist\": \"~delta\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 4.0\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elodea_cells_under_microscope.jpg\",\n      \"description\": \"Elodea leaf cells photographed under a microscope. Microscope preparation and resolution determine which features are visible.\"\n    },\n    \"animal-micrograph\": {\n      \"src\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Human_Cheek_Cells.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 640,\n      \"height\": 426,\n      \"title\": \"Human Cheek Cells.jpg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Light micrograph\",\n      \"artist\": \"Joseph Elsbernd (CodonAUG)\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Human_Cheek_Cells.jpg\",\n      \"description\": \"Human cheek cells stained with methylene blue; not an unstained natural-colour image.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"organisms\": {\n    \"homo-sapiens\": {\n      \"src\": \"/biology/reference/homo-sapiens.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 331,\n      \"height\": 554,\n      \"title\": \"Akha_cropped_hires.JPG\",\n      \"kind\": \"Organism reference image\",\n      \"artist\": \"Weltenbummler84\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 2.0 de\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/de/deed.en\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akha_cropped_hires.JPG\",\n      \"description\": \"Akha  couple in northern Thailand. The husband is carrying the stem of a banana-plant, which will be fed to their pigs.\"\n    },\n    \"felis-catus\": {\n      \"src\": \"/biology/reference/felis-catus.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 960,\n      \"height\": 978,\n      \"title\": \"Siam_lilacpoint.jpg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Organism reference image\",\n      \"artist\": \"Karin Langner-Bahmann , upload von  Martin Bahmann\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siam_lilacpoint.jpg\",\n      \"description\": \"8 month old  Siamese cat , with lilac points, facing right\"\n    },\n    \"capra-hircus\": {\n      \"src\": \"/biology/reference/capra-hircus.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 960,\n      \"height\": 960,\n      \"title\": \"Hausziege_04.jpg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Organism reference image\",\n      \"artist\": \"Kuebi  = Armin Kübelbeck\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hausziege_04.jpg\",\n      \"description\": \"Goat, located in Fiesch, Valais (Switzerland).\"\n    },\n    \"bos-taurus\": {\n      \"src\": \"/biology/reference/bos-taurus.jpg\",\n      \"width\": 960,\n      \"height\": 643,\n      \"title\": \"Cow_(Fleckvieh_breed)_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg\",\n      \"kind\": \"Organism reference image\",\n      \"artist\": \"Kim Hansen\",\n      \"license\": \"CC BY-SA 3.0\",\n      \"licenseUrl\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\",\n      \"source\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cow_(Fleckvieh_breed)_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg\",\n      \"description\": \"A dual breed (beef and milk) cow near  Oeschinen Lake ,  S